test_sleepy — sleeper child for the process-table exhaustion test
===================================================================

Phase 0c chunk 6 helper. Spawned by `test_procmax`; just blocks
in `nanosleep` long enough that the parent can stack a couple
dozen copies before any of them get reaped, then exits cleanly
if the parent ever forgets to kill it.

5 seconds is far longer than the headless QEMU test runtime
(<2 s post-boot) but short enough that a leaked instance
self-reaps before the next test boots. The parent always
`pm_kill`s + `pm_waitpid`s explicitly; this exit path is
belt-and-suspenders.

    module oskit.bin.test_sleepy

    import oskit.ulib.{exit, syscall6}


    val NR_NANOSLEEP = 251


    main(argv: []string)
        var ts: [16]byte
        ts[0] = byte(5)   // tv_sec = 5
        var i = 1
        while i < 16
            ts[i] = byte(0)
            i += 1
        syscall6(NR_NANOSLEEP, i64(&ts[0]), 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
        exit()
